  "scientific_scope_and_limitations": {
    "primary_axis": "Within-genome sensitivity to declared biomass template and medium recipes.",
    "optimality_caveat": "All min_added_rxns_count values are minima among found valid time-limited MILP solutions (heuristic_incumbent_bounded), not proven global minima. Weighted reaction costs allow counter-directional reaction-count differences under recipe relaxation.",
    "infeasibility_vs_unknown": "1,936 fixed-medium infeasible cases (all 484 genomes in S1/S2 minimal H2+CO2+NH4 under B0/B2) are separated from 66 numerical unknown cases (56 FBA verification failures, 10 timeouts with no incumbent) and 4 optional S0 unavailable cases (2 genomes with verified empty native/desert media). Fixed-medium infeasibility is never described as numerically unresolved, and neither category is coerced to zero added reactions.",
    "cohort_comparison_caveat": "Between-cohort comparisons are descriptive only. Even within the 455-genome CheckM2 method-family subset and 293-genome shared-order subset (o__JACQPN01, o__JACPAO01, o__SW-10-69-26), CheckM2 software versions/models may differ, deep-lineage structure within orders is not fully phylogeny-controlled, and no environmental adaptation claim is made. The 29 MGnify genomes have unknown quality assessment method and are kept strictly separate.",
    "masking_control_caveat": "Across the 7 selected high-completeness, low-contamination MGnify reference genomes (numeric >=90% completeness, <=5% contamination; formal MIMAG status unknown due to unrecorded rRNA/tRNA criteria; 9 nested masking conditions/replicates per genome = 63 evaluations), mean true masked GPR reaction recovery is 16.82% while alternative reactions account for 76.73% of newly induced additions. Gap-filling alone does not establish specific enzyme functions for dark proteins; these observations apply to the 7 tested reference genomes and are not generalized to all archaea."
  },
